# Dashboard card styling

When building or upgrading dashboard, overview, or command-center pages:

- **Every card must be color-coded** — no plain `bg-white` panels unless it is a nested item inside an already-colored card.
- Use **moderate tinted backgrounds** (not heavy saturation): gradients like `from-{tone}-100 via-{tone}-50 to-white` with `border-{tone}-200`, dark text (`text-{tone}-900`), and soft shadows (`shadow-md shadow-{tone}-200/20`).
- Assign a **distinct tone per card** (blue, emerald, purple, violet, orange, rose, cyan, amber, slate) so sections are scannable at a glance.
- Card headers should use a **slightly stronger tint** than the body (`border-b` + `bg-{tone}-100/70` on header).
- Nested metric tiles use `border-{tone}-200 bg-{tone}-50` with tone-matched dark text.
- Status badges use `border-{tone}-300 bg-{tone}-100 text-{tone}-800`.
- Page canvas must use a **white background** (`bg-white`) — cards remain the primary color carriers.

Reference implementation: `lib/dashboard-card-tones.ts` (`toneCard`, `toneCardHeader`, `toneMetric`, `toneTitle`, `toneBody`).
